<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sancha of León</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1018–1067</span> · Also known as Queen Sancha of León</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sancha was Queen of León, the daughter of Alfonso V and sister of Bermudo III, the last king of the old Leonese line. After her husband Ferdinand, count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>, killed Bermudo at Tamarón in 1037, he became king of León by right of her inheritance. She and Ferdinand I were patrons of the church of San Isidoro in León, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beatus-of-facundus">Beatus of Facundus</a> was made for them in 1047.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sancha-of-leon.jpg" alt="Sancha of León" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sheila1988 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sancha_of_Le%C3%B3n_statue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
